'''Aurocores''' (â-rok′ọ̄-rēz), ''n. pl.'' [NL., < L. ''aurum'', gold, + Gr. κόρις, a bug.] Literally, the gold-bugs; a group of heteropterous hemipterous insects, the same as ''Geocores'', the name ''Aurocores'' being considered more appropriate by Westwood, who proposed it as a substitute. See ''Geocores''.

'''Aurocorisa''' (â″rọ̄-kọ̄-rī′zä̤), ''n. pl.'' [NL.] Same as ''Aurocores''.

